- Wire EventAction and TrackingAction through ActionInitialization: event-local ancestry includes every tracked particle; event end creates both record vectors; next event clears state and aborted events produce no result rows. SD names come from constructed LMO volumes.
- User-confirmed policy: each detector has its own incident roots; descendants born there inherit the root, crossings into another detector start that detector's branch, in-detector primaries root at themselves, and re-entry of the same track is merged. A parent that never visited the target detector cannot establish a branch there.
- Reference review: LMO-Th232-sim/analyse/EnergyReconstruction.C recursively sums descendant tracks for each externally born candidate; separate roots in the same subtree can overlap. New recording assigns every detector/track deposit to exactly one root and preserves zero-deposit ancestors.
